  "result": "Perfect! All 56 tests pass. I've successfully added the two line-modification functions:\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n1. **Updated `src/errors.js`** \u2014 Added two new error codes:\n   - `NOT_DRAFT`: for modifying invoices that aren't in draft status\n   - `LINE_NOT_FOUND`: for removing a line that doesn't exist\n\n2. **Added `addLine(invoice, { sku, qty })`** to src/invoices.js:\n   - Validates invoice is in 'draft' status (NOT_DRAFT error)\n   - Validates qty is a positive integer (QTY_INVALID)\n   - Validates SKU exists (UNKNOWN_SKU)\n   - If SKU already exists on invoice, increases that line's qty\n   - Otherwise appends a new line with catalogue data\n   - Never mutates the original invoice\n\n3. **Added `removeLine(invoice, sku)`** to src/invoices.js:\n   - Validates invoice is in 'draft' status (NOT_DRAFT)\n   - Returns LINE_NOT_FOUND if SKU not on invoice\n   - Returns NO_LINES if removing it would leave the invoice empty\n   - Returns new invoice without that line\n   - Never mutates the original invoice\n\n4. **Added 16 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - Adding new lines and increasing qty\n   - Correct positioning when adding to multi-line invoices\n   - All error cases (invalid qty, unknown SKU, non-draft)\n   - Immutability guarantees\n   - Preventing removal of last line\n   - Chaining operations to build invoices incrementally\n\nAll 56 tests pass \u2713",
